{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "stress_balance",
    "description": "PISM stress-balance subassembly (stage 2 of the eqice project): the SIA and SSA stress-balance components of stage 2 mounted by reference and coupled into the shared StressBalance D-methods -- the assembled 2D velocity (ubar, vbar), the 3D velocity selection (u3, v3), the horizontal divergence and vertical velocity from incompressibility (div, w3), the volumetric strain heating (sigma), the basal frictional heating (F_b), and the SIA diffusive flux (q_x, q_y) -- reproducing the single-cell outputs of the instrumented PISM v2.3.2 runs (stage1/dumps/sia/, stage1/dumps/ssa/). The stress-balance model is selected at the CONFIG level in PISM 2.3.2 (stress_balance.model in {sia, ssa, ssa+sia, ...}, stressbalance/factory.cc): there is NO per-cell mask-based selection of the SIA vs SSA parts, so the numeric parameter sb_model encodes the config choice (0 = sia: ZeroSliding + SIAFD, ubar = 0 and u3 is the SIA profile; 1 = ssa: SSAFD + ConstantInColumn, ubar = u_ssa and u3 = ubar constant in the column; 2 = ssa+sia: SSAFD + SIAFD, ubar = u_ssa and the SIA profile rides on the SSA sliding velocity). The four staggered I(z) columns (SIADiffusivityColumn mounts at the east/west/north/south faces of the cell) drive both the SIA 3D velocity (SIA3DHorizontalVelocity mount, with the sliding velocity coupled from the assembled ubar/vbar) and the SIA diffusivity D (coupled into the SIADiffusiveFlux mount, giving the diffusive flux at the east staggered point); the SSA mount supplies the 2D velocity at the sampled cell (dump cell 29 = esm index 30 of the test-V flow line) through the literal-index coupling transform. The StressBalance assembler then computes, from the assembled 3D velocity field and the eight neighbor-column inputs: the divergence div = u_x + v_y with the mask-limited centered/one-sided stencils of StressBalance::compute_vertical_velocity (u_x = D_x*(west*(u - u_w) + east*(u_e - u)); the west/east/south/north weights are 0 across an ice margin, D_x = 1/(dx*(east+west))); the vertical velocity w3[k] = w3[k-1] - 0.5*dz*(div[k] + div[k-1]) with w3[0] = -bmr (bmr = 0 in all traces; the -bmr base term is deferred to stage 3, matching the leaf SIAVerticalVelocity); the volumetric strain heating sigma[k] = 2*e^(-1/n)*B[k]*D2[k]^(0.5*(1/n+1)) for k <= ks and 0 above, with D2 the strain-rate second invariant under the shallow approximations and B the Paterson-Budd-cold hardness; and the basal frictional heating F_b = 0 on ocean cells -- floating ice (3) or ice-free ocean (4), the mask.ocean skip of ShallowStressBalance::compute_basal_frictional_heating -- and C*(ubar^2 + vbar^2) otherwise, with the purely-plastic drag C = tauc/sqrt(eps^2 + ubar^2 + vbar^2) (basal_resistance.plastic.regularization = 0.01 m/yr = 3.1688764615412797e-10 m/s in the 31556926 s PISM year). Tests: (1) the grounded mid-radius cell (20,15) of the test-F grid, model = 0 -- the full I-chain to u3/v3 to div/w3/sigma assembly and the diffusive flux reproduce the dumped columns to machine precision; (2) the margin cell (27,15) whose east neighbor (28,15) is ice-free (mask 0) -- the one-sided x-stencil (east weight 0, west 1) and theta = 0.5 (BedSmoother trace) at the east staggered point; (3) the floating test-V cell 29, model = 1 -- ubar/u3 equal the SSA steady-state velocity at the sampled cell (rel 2e-3, the SSA leaf's steady-state tolerance story) and F_b = 0 (tauc = 0 on the shelf); (4) model = 2 wiring -- at t = 0 the SSA sits at its exact-solution warm start, so u3[2] = u_ic(30) + the sia-run shear at level 2; (5)-(7) synthetic F_b checks (tauc = 1e5 Pa, v_ssa = 1e-3 m/s) on grounded ice (mask 2: F_b = 100.03317883754333 W/m^2 by the drag formula), on ice-free ocean (mask 4: F_b = 0) and on floating ice (mask 3: F_b = 0 -- the mask.ocean skip covers floating cells too, a case the all-zero stage-1 F_b dumps cannot pin because the ssa run had tauc = 0 on the shelf). HARNESS FINDING (empirical): the coupled document -- top-level model refs + variable_map coupling -- loads, validates, and its inline tests RUN under `esm test` with the native compiler (47/47 pass; mounted components' tests are dropped at the mount per esm-spec 6.6, and the subassembly authors its own). Two native-compiler constraints shaped the equations: an ifelse whose branches have different value boxes (scalar vs indexed) is refused, so the ConstantInColumn selection works through lev-shaped ubar_col/vbar_col boxes; and index maps must be affine or constant selects, so the bed/interior switch of the vertical derivatives u_z/v_z is a makearray region split (the clamped formula is algebraically identical). Coupling limitations (documented per test): the eight neighbor 3D-velocity columns and the staggered-column inputs (thk/ks/E/alpha/theta and the surface gradients) are PARAMETERS here, sampled from the stage-1 dumps; in stage 3 they become full-grid couplings from the neighboring cells' SIA/SSA fields. Consequently the model = 1 (ssa) divergence/vertical-velocity values are NOT asserted (the constant-in-column field would need the neighbor inputs to be the SSA field as well), and in model = 2 the divergence computed with sia-run neighbor inputs carries the sliding-velocity jump across the cell (the D_x*ubar*(west - east) term) -- both deferred to the full-grid assembly. The strain-heating hardness uses the pressure-ADJUSTED temperature T_pa (PatersonBuddCold::softness_from_temp through FlowLaw::hardness_n) while the SIA flow factor of SIAFD::flow_n uses the ABSOLUTE temperature -- a C++ inconsistency of the reference, reproduced faithfully here (both branches verified against the stage-1 dumps; see the eqice bug list). While assembling this subassembly a genuine leaf-fidelity bug was found and fixed in sia.esm (the I(z) cumulative trapezoid above a staggered column's surface drifted by a partial top interval; SIAFD::compute_I fills the levels above the ice with an exact copy of the top in-ice value; the fix caps the I sum at j <= ks; all 48 sia.esm tests unchanged and green). theta (bed smoothness) remains an input (BedSmoother deferred to stage 3), and the SIA diffusive flux is exposed at the east staggered point only (the geometry step consumes all four faces in stage 3).",
    "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
    "tags": [
      "eqice:stage2",
      "pism:stress_balance",
      "coupling:subassembly"
    ]
  },
  "solver": {
    "stiffness": "high",
    "reltol": 1e-10,
    "abstol": 1e-13
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 61
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "SIAEast": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIADiffusivityColumn"
    },
    "SIAWest": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIADiffusivityColumn"
    },
    "SIANorth": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIADiffusivityColumn"
    },
    "SIASouth": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIADiffusivityColumn"
    },
    "SIAFlux": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIADiffusiveFlux"
    },
    "SIAVel": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIA3DHorizontalVelocity"
    },
    "SIAW": {
      "ref": "./sia.esm",
      "model": "SIAVerticalVelocity"
    },
    "SSA": {
      "ref": "./ssa.esm",
      "model": "SSAFlowline"
    },
    "StressBalance": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./stress_balance_templates.esm"
        },
        {
          "ref": "./ice_rheology_templates.esm"
        },
        {
          "ref": "./basal_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "sb_model": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Stress-balance model selector mirroring the PISM config stress_balance.model (stressbalance/factory.cc): 0 = sia (ZeroSliding + SIAFD), 1 = ssa (SSAFD + ConstantInColumn), 2 = ssa+sia (SSAFD + SIAFD). PISM 2.3.2 has no per-cell mask-based SIA/SSA selection."
        },
        "u_ssa": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "SSA 2D velocity at the sampled cell, coupled from the mounted flow line (SSA.u at esm index 30 = dump cell 29)."
        },
        "v_ssa": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "SSA 2D velocity y-component at the sampled cell (0 in the flow-line dumps; the synthetic F_b tests set it directly)."
        },
        "u3_sia": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "default": [0.0],
          "description": "SIA 3D velocity x-component (with sliding), coupled from the mounted SIA3DHorizontalVelocity."
        },
        "v3_sia": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "default": [0.0],
          "description": "SIA 3D velocity y-component (with sliding), coupled from the mounted SIA3DHorizontalVelocity."
        },
        "w3_sia": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "default": [0.0],
          "description": "Vertical velocity of the SIA part (trapezoid of -div), coupled from the mounted SIAVerticalVelocity."
        },
        "q_x_sia": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "SIA diffusive flux x-component at the east staggered point, coupled from the mounted SIADiffusiveFlux."
        },
        "q_y_sia": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "SIA diffusive flux y-component at the east staggered point, coupled from the mounted SIADiffusiveFlux."
        },
